.TH SIGTIMEDWAIT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
sigtimedwait \- waits for a signal in set, optionally with a timeout
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <signal.h>
.B int sigtimedwait(const sigset_t* set, siginfo_t* information, const struct timespec* timeout);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Waits for a signal in set, optionally with a timeout. siginfo_t uses the 128-byte Linux kernel layout, not libc's layout.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result on success, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sigtimedwait (2)
